WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.015
"The mayor might cancel the parade?" Henry exclaimed.

2
00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:23.701
"Why? Does he think that threat on the website was serious?

3
00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:27.506
Or did Mr. Fleming talk him into canceling the parade?"

4
00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:32.281
Jackson shrugged. "I don't know. I didn't hear it from the mayor.

5
00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:36.350
I was talking to Miss Bishop. She's the one who told me."

6
00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:39.854
"How did she hear about it?" Henry asked.

7
00:00:39.855 --> 00:00:45.287
"I'm not sure. I couldn't talk to her for very long because I had to leave for a meeting."

8
00:00:45.288 --> 00:00:47.504
Jackson checked his watch.

9
00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:51.425
"Speaking of which, I've got to get inside or I'll be late."

10
00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:54.559
He hurried into the newspaper office.

11
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.479
Henry thought about what Jackson had just said.

12
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.026
Should Miss Bishop be a suspect?

13
00:01:00.027 --> 00:01:03.844
She seemed determined to win the contest for best float.

14
00:01:03.845 --> 00:01:07.479
She seemed especially interested in beating Mrs. Sweet.

15
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.525
Could Miss Bishop be the one who'd tampered with Mrs. Sweet's float?

16
00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:15.021
Then Henry remembered the threatening website message.

17
00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:17.971
Why would Miss Bishop do something like that?

18
00:01:17.972 --> 00:01:23.251
If she wanted to win, it didn't make sense for her to try to shut down the whole parade.

19
00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:26.385
Henry started walking his bike down the sidewalk.

20
00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:31.679
The jewelry store was up ahead. He decided to stop in and talk to Miss Bishop.

21
00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.824
A little bell over the door jingled when Henry entered the jewelry store.

22
00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:39.983
Nobody was inside except Miss Bishop.

23
00:01:39.984 --> 00:01:43.049
She was wiping a display case with a rag.

24
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.419
"Oh, hello, Henry," she said.

25
00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.150
"Did you come to buy your mother a diamond necklace?"

26
00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:54.327
Henry smiled politely as Miss Bishop laughed at her own joke.

27
00:01:54.328 --> 00:01:56.805
"No, sorry," he said.

28
00:01:56.806 --> 00:02:01.267
"Our lemonade business doesn't make quite enough money for that."

29
00:02:01.268 --> 00:02:05.967
"Too bad." Miss Bishop smiled, and then sighed.

30
00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:11.780
"I could really use some new customers. Business has been slow this summer."

31
00:02:11.781 --> 00:02:15.743
"Oh," Henry said. "That's a shame."

32
00:02:15.744 --> 00:02:21.731
"Yes, that's why I decided to enter a float in the parade this year," Miss Bishop said.

33
00:02:21.732 --> 00:02:24.243
"I thought it would be good publicity.

34
00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:28.987
And if I win the popular vote contest, I'll get to be on TV.

35
00:02:28.988 --> 00:02:32.278
That's like winning a free ad for my store."

36
00:02:32.279 --> 00:02:37.473
"You must be worried about the mayor canceling the parade then," Henry said.

37
00:02:37.474 --> 00:02:40.485
"What?" Miss Bishop looked alarmed.

38
00:02:40.486 --> 00:02:44.514
"The mayor is canceling the parade? Who told you that?"

39
00:02:44.515 --> 00:02:48.798
"Jackson, the reporter from the newspaper," Henry said.

40
00:02:48.799 --> 00:02:50.838
"He said you told him that."

41
00:02:50.839 --> 00:02:55.147
"I told him no such thing!" Miss Bishop exclaimed.

42
00:02:55.148 --> 00:02:59.212
"He must be thinking of someone else. Do you think it's true?

43
00:02:59.213 --> 00:03:02.114
Why would the mayor cancel the parade?"

44
00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:05.119
Henry wasn't sure what to say for a moment.

45
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.098
He was confused by Miss Bishop's reaction.

46
00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:11.007
She seemed very surprised and upset.

47
00:03:11.008 --> 00:03:15.691
"Was Jackson here talking to you earlier?" Henry asked.

48
00:03:15.692 --> 00:03:17.409
Miss Bishop nodded.

49
00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:22.580
"Yes, he stopped by a few minutes ago, and we had a nice chat.

50
00:03:22.581 --> 00:03:25.863
I was telling him about my business problems."

51
00:03:25.864 --> 00:03:30.177
"And you didn't say anything about the parade?" Henry asked.

52
00:03:30.178 --> 00:03:37.840
"I did mention the parade, but I didn't say anything about the mayor canceling it," Miss Bishop said.

53
00:03:37.841 --> 00:03:42.608
"I told Jackson that I was hoping my float would bring me more customers.

54
00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:46.389
And that if it didn't, I might have to shut down my store."

55
00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:52.532
"Oh." Suddenly Henry had a brainstorm. "I bet I know what happened.

56
00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:56.764
You told Jackson you might have to shut down your store.

57
00:03:56.765 --> 00:04:01.589
But Jackson thought you were talking about the mayor shutting down the parade."

58
00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.989
"Hmm." Miss Bishop looked unsure. "That seems odd.

59
00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:15.127
But Jackson did seem to be in a hurry. Maybe he wasn't listening closely."

60
00:04:15.128 --> 00:04:21.093
As Henry left the store, he wondered if Jackson had really misunderstood Miss Bishop's comment.

61
00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:25.333
The young reporter was always looking for exciting news stories.

62
00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:29.024
What if he was the one trying to get the parade shut down?

63
00:04:29.025 --> 00:04:33.262
That would definitely give Jackson an interesting story to write about.

64
00:04:33.263 --> 00:04:37.763
Henry thought some more about his theory as he biked toward Maggie's house.

65
00:04:37.764 --> 00:04:43.169
Jackson could have posted that threatening message on the website just as easily as anyone else.

66
00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.929
He could have broken into Mrs. Sweet's shed.

67
00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:55.976
And he was definitely the one spreading the rumor about the parade being canceled—either by accident or on purpose.

68
00:04:55.977 --> 00:05:01.255
When Henry reached Maggie's house, Maggie and Cole were putting away their craft supplies.

69
00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:04.641
"What took you so long?" Maggie asked Henry.

70
00:05:04.642 --> 00:05:08.795
"It's dinnertime. We'll have to finish the float in the morning."

71
00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:11.124
"Sorry," Henry said.

72
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:16.231
"I ended up doing a little extra investigating on my way home from the auto shop."

73
00:05:16.232 --> 00:05:19.258
He told his friends about his trip to town.

74
00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:24.422
When he explained his theory about Jackson being the culprit, Cole looked worried.

75
00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:30.597
"If Jackson is a suspect now, we can't count on him to solve the mystery," he said.

76
00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:35.139
Henry nodded. "You know what that means," he said.

77
00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:39.933
"We'll have to solve it ourselves!"
